Hi all,=20

I'm trying to use my pc as a voice gateway I mean that I've a bluetooth =
connection between my pc and my phone and  instead of having sound going =
in and out of the phone, I want it to go in and out of the micro and the =
pc speakers. Have anyone already done this? All I was able to do is to =
establish a bluetooth connection between my nokia N70 and the pc running =
ubuntu using a belkin dongle. Then when a call is coming, the N70 begins =
to ring and I got a bluetooth connection with the icon of a headset. =
Althougth when I hang up I dont hear nothing neither from the pc nor =
from the nokia N70, the absolute silence. I'm using btsco and I've =
chosen alsa as a sound driver. My pc works as a voice gateway under =
windows and I got sound out of my pc speakers so why linux can't provide =
the same behaviour??=20

Hope that you can help me.=20

Thanks a lot.

